invariant: INV-7
file: handshake_parser.c
catches: webpki_session_test
reason: the parser takes a HelloRetryRequest whose key_share names x25519,
  a group the webpki hello already carried a share for, and the client
  resends the same hello. RFC 9846 section 4.3.8 makes a retry naming a
  shared group an illegal_parameter at the retry itself, and a server
  could loop the client or treat the resent hello as a change it never
  asked for.

--- old
        // illegal_parameter abort (rfc9846.txt:2205-2212).
        return CH_EPROTO;
    }
--- new
        // illegal_parameter abort (rfc9846.txt:2205-2212).
        return rb_u16(e) == CH_GROUP_X25519 ? CH_OK : CH_EPROTO;
    }
